------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 1 -- what alpha_1 DOES: the signature algebra
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    .  k->0: -4*up/(up - 1)   k->inf: 0   u'->0: 0   asymptote: 8/(Ls**2*k2)
K3 PASS  value=-4*up/(up - 1), 0, 0, 8/(Ls**2*k2)  threshold=4u'/(1-u'), 0, 0, 8/(kL*)^2   [alpha_1 is screened BOTH by high acceleration (u'->0) and by a source small compared with L* (kL*>>1); it is O(1) only for g~a0 AND r_s >> L*]
    .  alpha_1 = 1    at g/a0 = 1.236   (analytic 1/sqrt(0.2)-1 = 1.236)
    .  alpha_1 = 1e-4 at g/a0 = 199.00  (analytic 1/sqrt(2.5e-5)-1 = 199.00)
K4 PASS  value=1.236, 199.00 a0  threshold=1.236, 199.0 a0   [alpha_1 = 4u'/(1-u'): unity at 1.24 a0, the PPN line 1e-4 at 199 a0]
    .  alpha_1(g), r_s >> L*: 1e22a0:4.0e-44, 1e21a0:4.0e-42, 1e20a0:4.0e-40, 1e19a0:4.0e-38, 1e18a0:4.0e-36 ...  1e-2a0:1.99e+02
K5 PASS  value=monotone=True, span=45.7 decades  threshold=monotone, > 40   [alpha_1 spans 46 decades between a neutron-star surface and a galaxy: it is not a PPN parameter, it is a response function]
    .  crossing at r_s = L*: g* = 199.0 a0 = 1.863e-08 m/s^2
    .  crossing at r_s = 1 pc: 198.3 a0; at 8 kpc: 199.0 a0; at 20 kAU: 95.8 a0
    .  max over g: 20 kAU -> 1.31e-04 (= 8(r/L*)^2 = 1.31e-04); 18 AU -> 1.1e-10
K6 PASS  value=199.0 a0, 198.3 a0, r_x=17502 AU, max(20kAU)=1.3e-04, max(18AU)=1.1e-10  threshold=199 a0, 199 a0, 17502 AU, >1e-4, <1e-6   [the 1e-4 line is a LOCUS: 199 a0 for any source larger than ~1 pc, 96 a0 at 20 kAU, and unreachable (max 8(r_s/L*)^2) below 17.5 kAU]
    .  v1.v2 = Vx**2 - Vx*m1*ux/(m1 + m2) + Vx*m2*ux/(m1 + m2) + Vy**2 - Vy*m1*uy/(m1 + m2) + Vy*m2*uy/(m1 + m2) + Vz**2 - Vz*m1*uz/(m1 + m2) + Vz*m2*uz/(m1 + m2) - m1*m2*ux**2/(m1**2 + 2*m1*m2 + m2**2) - m1*m2*uy**2/(m1**2 + 2*m1*m2 + m2**2) - m1*m2*uz**2/(m1**2 + 2*m1*m2 + m2**2)
K7 PASS  value=residual=0, velocity-independent terms=0  threshold=0, 0   [the alpha_1 Lagrangian is BILINEAR in velocities: every alpha_1 observable carries (v/c)^2 with v in {V, u}. There is no alpha_1 effect at zeroth order in velocity.]
    .  dL/du = [-Gsec*M*Vx*alpha1*m/(2*r), -Gsec*M*Vy*alpha1*m/(2*r), -Gsec*M*Vz*alpha1*m/(2*r)]
    .  dL/dr  = Gsec*M*alpha1*m*(Vx**2 + Vx*ux + Vy**2 + Vy*uy + Vz**2 + Vz*uz)/(2*r**2)
K8 PASS  value=sum of component residuals = 0  threshold=0   [preferred-frame acceleration: (alpha1/2)(GM/c^2)[V rdot - (V^2+V.u)rhat]/r^2 -- a V^2 piece (uniform G rescaling, absorbable) plus a V.u piece (velocity-dependent), verified in all three components]
    .  at 8 kpc, v_rot = 220 km/s: monopole (w/c)^2 = 1.52e-06, dipole 2(w/c)(v/c) = 1.81e-06, v^2 (v/c)^2 = 5.39e-07
K9 PASS  value=residual = 0  threshold=0   [the monopole piece is exactly degenerate with the mass (a G-rescaling IS a M-rescaling): only the dipole and v^2 pieces are observable in one system]

